(NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7283) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n1. When mouse moving over CollisionObject3D, signals `mouse_entered` and `mouse_exited` are fired.\nBut then mouse is **drag** over CollisionObject3D,  signals `mouse_entered` and `mouse_exited` are **NOT** fired.\n\n2.  Signal  `mouse_exited` fired only **on mouse button release** not on exiting actual collision shape border\n\nVideo with issue on `Windows`:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3e1aa379-de8b-4059-923c-0f57684163b5\n\nOn `Android` there are no issue:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ac7fed9-9929-4467-aade-3a39984ae736\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create `Area3D`\n2. Add `CollisionShape3D`\n3. Set shape `BoxShape`\n4. Connect signals  `mouse_entered` and `mouse_exited` for Area3D\n5. Add some notification to signals\n6. Drag mouse over CollisionShape\n\nOption `input / Capture on Drag` for `Area3D` doesn't change anything.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[incorrect-behavior.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23841941/incorrect-behavior.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113374/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}